      "side": 1,
      "message": "**Endianness Vulnerability in Command Construction (`ft_scsi.cc`)** You correctly apply `htole32` to the CBW tag and signature. However, in `BuildFtCmd`, you directly assign `uint32_t` values to the `FtCmdFormat` struct.\n\n```c\nFtCmdFormat cmd{\n  .opcode \u003d opcode,\n  .address \u003d address, // \u003c-- Host-endian assignment\n  .length \u003d length,\n  // ...\n};\nreturn std::bit_cast\u003cstd::array\u003cuint8_t, 16\u003e\u003e(cmd);\n\n```\n\nWhile ChromiumOS predominantly runs on little-endian architectures (where host-endian matches USB-endian), directly passing host-endian structures violates USB specifications and breaks portability.\n\n* **Recommendation:** Wrap these fields in `htole32()`.\n\n```c\n.address \u003d htole32(address),\n.length \u003d htole32(length),\n.aux_address \u003d htole32(aux_address),\n\n```",
