      "message": "Flagged by Gemini:\n\n----\n\n**Data Truncation Bug in Payload Padding (`updater.cc`)** In `FtDownloadBin`, the calculation to pad the remaining payload to a 4-byte boundary unintentionally truncates the buffer length instead of aligning it.\n\n```c\n// Current Code\nif (len \u003e 0) {\n  len \u003d FtDivRoundUp\u003csize_t\u003e(len, 4); // \u003c--- Converts byte count to word count!\n  auto page_res \u003d FtDownloadPage(device, downaddr, len, {p, len});\n  ...\n}\n\n```\n\nBecause `len` is modified to represent the *number of words*, the `{p, len}` span construction only captures a fraction of the remaining bytes. For example, if 3 bytes are remaining, `len` becomes 1, and only 1 byte is flashed.\n\n* **Recommendation:** Multiply the rounded value back by 4 to maintain byte-length semantics, or use a proper alignment macro.\n\n```c\nlen \u003d FtDivRoundUp\u003csize_t\u003e(len, 4) * 4;\n\n```\n\n*(Note: Based on your `total_frame` logic, `len` will almost always perfectly zero out before this block anyway, but this guard needs to be functionally correct).*",
