      "message": "Here is Gemini generated code to add a test case to cover this issue. Verify for correctness:\n\n----\n\nHere are the concrete changes to implement both the fix and the test case, along with the rationale for why this approach is the most robust.\n\n### The Rationale\n\n**1. The Root Cause (The Bug)**\nIn C++ `std::ifstream`, when you attempt to read `N` bytes but the file only contains `N - 1` bytes, the stream hits the End-Of-File marker. This sets *both* the `failbit` and the `eofbit`.\n\nIn the original patch, the error handling logic in `IsEcBinHasConfigPage` was:\n`if (!file.good() \u0026\u0026 !file.eof())`\n\nBecause `file.eof()` evaluates to `true`, the `!file.eof()` condition evaluates to `false`. The entire `if` statement is bypassed. The code proceeds to evaluate `config.code_valid_control_word`, which is sitting on the stack and contains uninitialized garbage data, leading to unpredictable behavior or silent memory corruption.\n\n**2. The Fix**\nRelying on state flags (`good()`, `eof()`, `fail()`) when doing binary block reads is often brittle. The safest and most explicit way to verify a binary read is to ask the stream exactly how many bytes it successfully extracted using `file.gcount()`. If it didn\u0027t extract exactly `sizeof(config)`, the file is invalid.\n\n**3. The Test Case**\nWe use `sizeof(FtConfigPage) - 1` to create an off-by-one edge case. If the logic is ever reverted or accidentally modified to only check `\u003e 0` bytes, this test will catch it. We route this through `UpdateFw` to ensure the entire firmware update pipeline properly rejects malformed files before interacting with the USB hardware.\n\n---\n\n### The Code Changes\n\nApply the following modifications to your original patch:\n\n#### 1. Fix the reading logic in `util/focaltech/updater.cc`\n\n```diff\n--- a/util/focaltech/updater.cc\n+++ b/util/focaltech/updater.cc\n@@ -235,8 +235,8 @@\n \n   FtConfigPage config{};\n   file.read(reinterpret_cast\u003cchar*\u003e(\u0026config), sizeof(config));\n-  if (!file.good() \u0026\u0026 !file.eof()) {\n-    FT_LOGE(\"Failed to read config page\");\n+  if (file.gcount() !\u003d sizeof(config)) {\n+    FT_LOGE(\"Failed to read config page (file too small)\");\n     return std::unexpected(FtError::kResultFail);\n   }\n \n\n```\n\n#### 2. Add the test case to `util/focaltech/updater_test.cc`\n\n```diff\n--- a/util/focaltech/updater_test.cc\n+++ b/util/focaltech/updater_test.cc\n@@ -193,6 +193,22 @@\n   EXPECT_EQ(res.error(), FtError::kParameterError);\n }\n \n+TEST(UpdaterTest, UpdateFw_FailsOnFileTooSmall) {\n+  // Create a payload strictly 1 byte smaller than required to test EOF handling\n+  std::vector\u003cuint8_t\u003e undersized_data(sizeof(FtConfigPage) - 1, 0xFF);\n+  ScopedTempFile fw_file(undersized_data);\n+  std::string fw_path \u003d fw_file.path();\n+\n+  auto transport \u003d std::make_unique\u003cStubUsbTransport\u003e();\n+  UsbDevice device(std::move(transport));\n+\n+  FtDeviceInfo info{.current_mode \u003d FtDeviceMode::kBoot, .ec_bin \u003d fw_path};\n+\n+  auto res \u003d UpdateFw(device, info);\n+  \n+  EXPECT_FALSE(res.has_value());\n+  EXPECT_EQ(res.error(), FtError::kResultFail);\n+}\n+\n TEST(UpdaterTest, UpdateFw_FailsOnModeMismatch) {\n   FtConfigPage config{.code_valid_control_word \u003d kCodeValidMagic,\n\n```",
